      <h1 class="font-serif-sc text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-stone-900 mt-3">
        The Zhongshan Suit: Revolutionary Elegance
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-stone-500 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        Known internationally as the Mao suit, the Zhongshan suit was actually designed by Dr. Sun Yat-sen (Sun Zhongshan) in the early 20th century as a modern, distinctly Chinese alternative to Western suits. With its four patch pockets, turned-down collar, and clean military-inspired lines, it became the uniform of China''s revolutionary era — and today, it''s experiencing a quiet revival among style-conscious travelers.
      </p>

