      <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">Design & Symbolism</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">Every element of the Zhongshan suit carries meaning. The four outer pockets represent the Four Virtues: propriety, righteousness, honesty, and shame. The five center-front buttons symbolize the five branches of government from Sun Yat-sen''s political philosophy. The three cuff buttons stand for the Three Principles of the People: nationalism, democracy, and people''s livelihood. The turned-down collar replaced the mandarin collar to signal modernity. The result is a garment that''s both deeply symbolic and remarkably wearable — a fitted jacket with practical pockets that moves comfortably.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">Where to Get One</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">Nanjing — Sun Yat-sen''s capital — is the spiritual home of the Zhongshan suit. Heritage tailor houses near the Presidential Palace still cut these suits using mid-century patterns and techniques. Guangzhou, Sun Yat-sen''s birthplace, has tailors who specialize in lighter, southern-adapted versions in breathable linens and cottons. A custom Zhongshan suit costs 500-1,200 RMB and takes 5-7 days. Off-the-rack versions are available for 200-400 RMB. For the best experience, visit a Nanjing tailor on day one of your trip and return for the final fitting before you leave.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">How to Wear It Today</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">The Zhongshan suit is surprisingly versatile. Wear it as a full suit for formal occasions, or pair the jacket with chinos for a smart-casual look. Dark navy and charcoal are the most wearable colors. Avoid the olive-green versions sold at tourist markets — they''re costume-quality. A properly tailored Zhongshan suit in midnight blue wool is indistinguishable from high-end tailoring and draws compliments wherever you wear it. Many travelers report it''s the single best souvenir they brought back from China.</p>
